{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "legend",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Legend**\n\ud83d\udfe9 done \u00b7 \ud83d\udfe8 now \u00b7 \u2b1c taught, not studied \u00b7 \ud83d\udfe5 not taught yet \u00b7 \ud83d\udfea midterm scope (in only if cumulative) \u00b7 \ud83d\udfe7 shaky\nBuilt from the COURSE OUTLINE (27 Oct). Updated as material lands.\nH = Horngren 17e \u00b7 M = Monvika 10e (Thai)",
			"x": 0,
			"y": -280,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 210
		},
		{
			"id": "ohs1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Plantwide rate**\none rate for the whole factory",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "ohs2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Departmental rates**\none rate per department, each on its own driver\nValidated 15 Nov (constructed, no real-paper version found in the 2021 final): Cutting $20/machine-hr, Finishing $30/labor-hr, Job #101 applied OH = $1,600 ($1,000 + $600). Clean, first try, no misses.",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 200,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "ohs3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Activity-based costing (ABC)**\ncost pools \u2192 drivers \u2192 products \u00b7 who's under- or over-costed\nPast: 2021 final Q2 (undercosting)\nValidated 14 Nov: Mary Inc. plantwide-vs-ABC batch calc, correct (undercosted under plantwide: $4.00 vs $6.55/unit).",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 400,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "oh",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Overhead allocation\nsessions 8\u20139 (28 Sep, 5 Oct) \u00b7 H Ch 5 \u00b7 M Ch 4",
			"x": 400,
			"y": 205,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 160
		},
		{
			"id": "sds1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Direct method**\nignore support-to-support services",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 720,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "sds2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Step-down method**\nthe order you allocate in changes the answer\nValidated 14 Nov: Betty's Book/Music full 2-step calc (Warehouse first by %-to-other-support-dept rule, then DC pool incl. closed-Warehouse trap), landed $126,649 correct after guided build.",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 920,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "sds3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Reciprocal method**\nsimultaneous equations: full support-to-support\nValidated 15 Nov: Betty's Book/Music real past-paper data, full reciprocal solve (equation setup + both totals + allocation to Music $449,134 / Books $325,866, checksum exact to $775,000). Misses: grabbed wrong usage row first (matched dept to wrong metric), misread 'X% x DC' as a % increase on W's own number rather than a share of DC's unknown total \u2014 both ghosted.",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 1120,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "sd",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Support-department costs\nsession 10 (12 Oct) \u00b7 H Ch 16 \u00b7 M Ch 5",
			"x": 400,
			"y": 925,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 160
		},
		{
			"id": "vas1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**What goes into product cost**\nthe whole difference = fixed MOH",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 1440,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "vas2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Why the profits differ**\nchange in inventory \u00d7 fixed MOH per unit \u00b7 reconcile the two\nValidated 14 Nov: Andrea Q11/Q12 (gross margin $24,750, operating income $16,500), correct after fixing the period-vs-product-cost mixup.",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 1640,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "va",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Variable vs absorption costing\nsession 11 (19 Oct) \u00b7 H Ch 9 \u00b7 M Ch 8",
			"x": 400,
			"y": 1545,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 160
		},
		{
			"id": "scs1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Materials**\nprice \u00b7 quantity (efficiency) \u00b7 **mix & yield**\nPast: 2021 final Q3 (standard costing)\nValidated 14 Nov: mix (70/30->60/40 rubber, direction) + combined real past-paper Q (Product X, mix $500F / yield $1,211U) \u2014 self-corrected live, caught own 'mix and yield move together' assumption.",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 1960,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "scs2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Labour**\nrate \u00b7 efficiency\nValidated 14 Nov: TU Corp labor rate variance via 3-pillar method (AQ\u00d7AP vs AQ\u00d7SP vs SQ\u00d7SP), Cr $7,014 correct, self-built the pillars.",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 2160,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "scs3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Manufacturing overhead**\nvariable: spending \u00b7 efficiency\nfixed: spending (budget) \u00b7 production-volume\nALL FOUR now validated on real/constructed numbers. 14 Nov: Zelma Inc. real past-paper Q (favorable VOH efficiency), correct via 3-column map. 15 Nov: Matthew's Corp real past-paper Q (flexible-budget fixed OH = $120,000 since fixed costs don't flex; production-volume variance $20,000 U), clean after a units mix-up on hrs/unit. 15 Nov: variable OH spending variance $700 U (caught using std hrs instead of actual hrs \u2014 real miss, ghosted) and fixed OH spending variance $6,500 U (clean, first try). Every OH sub-variance now tested at least once.",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 2360,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "sc",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Standard costing & variances\nsessions 12\u201315 (26 Oct \u2192 16 Nov) \u00b7 BEING TAUGHT\nH Ch 7\u20138 \u00b7 M Ch 7\n4 of the 8 sessions \u2192 probably the biggest share (guess)\n14 Nov: all 3 sub-blocks (materials incl. mix/yield, labour, overhead) validated against real 2021 past-paper Qs in one session.",
			"x": 400,
			"y": 2165,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "mt",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Midterm scope (sessions 1\u20137)\nfundamentals \u00b7 job order \u00b7 process costing \u00b7 joint & byproducts\nin the final ONLY if it's cumulative \u2192 ask",
			"x": 400,
			"y": 2585,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 160,
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "root",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "# AC313 Final\n40% \u00b7 **Mon 23 Nov, 09:00\u201312:00**\nTHE FIRST FINAL of the window (27 days)\nScope isn't stated in the outline: assume sessions 8\u201315 (guess, ask her)\nQuizzes & assignments = 20%",
			"x": -80,
			"y": 1250,
			"width": 400,
			"height": 280
		},
		{
			"id": "res",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Resources**\nDrive (a senior's, in `~/Desktop/pastpapers/AC313/`):\n\u00b7 `AC313 Final2021.pdf` = 45 pages of screenshots of the 2021 ONLINE final (MCQ, 2 points each) + a worked copy\n  \u26a0 no OCR on the Mac \u2192 Crow reads it page by page when we study\n\u00b7 old AC203 midterm (AC203 = AC313's old code)\nOn disk: Course Package 1 (midterm half) + **Package 2 + Exercise 2 (added 3 Nov)** in `~/Desktop/AC313/`",
